## Interface: 100007, 16001
## Title: |cff888888Spoken Quests (now in Spoken)|r
## Notes: Spoken Quests is now part of Spoken, in the Spoken_Quests folder. This folder never loads and is safe to delete.
## Version: 3.2.0-alpha.1
## Group: Spoken
## LoadOnDemand: 1
# A tombstone, with no Lua. Spoken Quests shipped in this folder until 3.0.0-beta.3, which moved
# it to Spoken_Quests: the name SpokenQuests belongs to the retired CurseForge project of the
# same name, and the CurseForge app updating or removing a stale install of that project would
# otherwise overwrite or delete the folder Spoken's own download ships the module in.
# scripts/spoken/package-retired.sh writes this file over every .toc name the old folder had on
# Blizzard's clients, each with that client's Interface line (scripts/lib/tombstone.sh), as that
# project's last release, and the 1.12, 2.4.3 and 3.3.5 zips carry it over the one .toc those
# clients read (scripts/quests/package.sh). Either way the old copy is left with nothing to
# load, rather than loading beside Spoken_Quests and voicing every line twice. LoadOnDemand
# keeps the client from loading even the empty addon, which is also what keeps Spoken's
# leftover-folder warning (OLD_FOLDERS in addons/Spoken/Core.lua) quiet: it names only a full
# old copy, which does load.
